It is Friday after work and I go to a small bakery.
I see many delicious cakes in the window.
A small fruit tart looks particularly good.
I hope that it will taste good to Nele.
The baker greets me in a friendly way.
"What can I get you?" he asks.
"I would like the small fruit tart, please," I say.
He carefully puts the cake into a light cardboard box.
"That makes six euros, please," says the baker.
I pay and he gives me the receipt.
"Thank you and have a nice weekend," he says.
"Thank you, to you too," I answer.
I step out of the bakery with the box.
First, I want to put the box into my backpack.
But I know that the cake will break in the backpack.
So I will carry the delicate box flat in my hands.
That way, the fruit tart stays safe.
Now I walk carefully to the U-Bahn.
